M Usage statement that related work is described only at the level of the cited titles. || evidence=references_provenance.json entries for Broderick2020AnAF and 2501.17858 (title, year, venue only); claims_grounding.json claims for ref.s2.f4c5a3ee... and ref.openalex.W4406975857. || fix=Remove the three unsupported descriptors. Describe Broderick et al. only as proposing a finite-sample robustness metric for when dropping a little data changes conclusions. Describe the vote-rigging paper only as studying vote-rigging strategies against Chatbot Arena and their effect on rankings, without stating what manipulations its setting allows.\nAUDIT_FINDING: id=runtime-claim-misattributed || section=Discussion (Implications for practice); Supplement (Data provenance and reproduction) || claim=A one-shot influence ranking plus bisection over exact refits certifies small reversal budgets on tables of this size in seconds on a CPU. || issue=The only timing evidence is 4.45 s and 4.51 s per held-out episode for the full studied configuration. That configuration includes re-linearisation and polish, and the episodes cover all six cases. No timing exists for a one-shot influence ranking with bisection. The hardware is not recorded in the evidence, so 'on a CPU' is unsupported. This also depends on the unverified B2 construction. || evidence=paper_data.json final_evaluation episodes duration_seconds 4.452 and 4.508; claims_grounding.json claim 6 (durations for the studied configuration only); the paper says B2's construction is not verified. || fix=Say that the studied configuration's recorded held-out evaluation episodes took about 4.5 s each, and remove the 'one-shot ranking plus bisection' attribution and the 'on a CPU' wording."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":90161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180},